# calc_flashover.py  CALCULATION (T-060, CR-002; T-096 SMD 3k3)
# IEC source 150 pF / 330 ohm, R = 3.3 kOhm +1 % = 3333 ohm; V_gap = V * R / (R + 330)
#   nominal 3k3: V_gap(4 kV) = 3636 V; R +1 %: 3640 V
#   nominal 3k3: V_gap(8 kV) = 7273 V; R +1 %: 7279 V

== IEC contact 4 kV: V_gap = 3640 V (CALCULATION); peak current with arc bypassing R = 12.1 A (= V / 330 ohm), with R in circuit = 1.09 A
  M1 uniform 2.0 kV/mm                       required gap   1.82 mm
  M1 uniform 2.5 kV/mm                       required gap   1.46 mm
  M1 uniform 3.0 kV/mm                       required gap   1.21 mm
  M1 uniform 3.5 kV/mm                       required gap   1.04 mm
  M1 uniform 4.5 kV/mm                       required gap   0.81 mm
  M2 Paschen (Townsend form)                 required gap   0.67 mm
  M3 empirical uniform air                   required gap   0.73 mm
  M4 non-uniform eta=0.7                     required gap   1.17 mm
  M4 non-uniform eta=0.5                     required gap   1.79 mm
  M4 non-uniform eta=0.3                     required gap   3.33 mm
  M5 IEC 60664-1 F.2 case B (homog.)         required gap   1.04 mm
  M5 IEC 60664-1 F.2 case A (inhomog.)       required gap   2.61 mm
  M5 F.2 case A at the full level            required gap   3.00 mm

== IEC contact 8 kV: V_gap = 7279 V (CALCULATION); peak current with arc bypassing R = 24.2 A (= V / 330 ohm), with R in circuit = 2.18 A
  M1 uniform 2.0 kV/mm                       required gap   3.64 mm
  M1 uniform 2.5 kV/mm                       required gap   2.91 mm
  M1 uniform 3.0 kV/mm                       required gap   2.43 mm
  M1 uniform 3.5 kV/mm                       required gap   2.08 mm
  M1 uniform 4.5 kV/mm                       required gap   1.62 mm
  M2 Paschen (Townsend form)                 required gap   1.56 mm
  M3 empirical uniform air                   required gap   1.79 mm
  M4 non-uniform eta=0.7                     required gap   2.77 mm
  M4 non-uniform eta=0.5                     required gap   4.14 mm
  M4 non-uniform eta=0.3                     required gap   7.46 mm
  M5 IEC 60664-1 F.2 case B (homog.)         required gap   2.63 mm
  M5 IEC 60664-1 F.2 case A (inhomog.)       required gap   7.07 mm
  M5 F.2 case A at the full level            required gap   8.00 mm

# Check of the models at known points (sanity, CALCULATION):
  d =   0.5 mm: Paschen   2880 V   empirical   2746 V   (textbook: ~4.5 kV at 1 mm, ~30 kV at 10 mm)
  d =   1.0 mm: Paschen   5035 V   empirical   4606 V   (textbook: ~4.5 kV at 1 mm, ~30 kV at 10 mm)
  d =   2.0 mm: Paschen   8945 V   empirical   7960 V   (textbook: ~4.5 kV at 1 mm, ~30 kV at 10 mm)
  d =   5.0 mm: Paschen  19483 V   empirical  17121 V   (textbook: ~4.5 kV at 1 mm, ~30 kV at 10 mm)
  d =  10.0 mm: Paschen  35509 V   empirical  31440 V   (textbook: ~4.5 kV at 1 mm, ~30 kV at 10 mm)

# SMD board (T-091): 2512 land copper gap 5.00 mm (CALCULATION (design file), check_smd.out); RC2512 termination gap min 4.65 mm
#   (CALCULATION from YAGEO RC_L V.11 L and I1); worst termination pair over placement error in check_gap.out (d).
  4 kV: V_gap 3640 V vs B min 4.65 mm: uniform 3 kV/mm withstands 13950 V, IEC F.2 case A needs 2.61 mm -> below the gap
  8 kV: V_gap 7279 V vs B min 4.65 mm: uniform 3 kV/mm withstands 13950 V, IEC F.2 case A needs 7.07 mm -> EXCEEDS the gap

DESIGN RULE (a) ELEx <-> Ex same channel, copper and leads:  gap >= 3.5 mm  (4 kV, worst of M4 eta=0.3 3.33 mm and IEC F.2 case A at 4 kV 3.00 mm, rounded up)
DESIGN RULE (b) Ex <-> ELEy any other channel (and any MPR121 / Pico net): gap >= 3.5 mm (same V_gap)
REPORTED 8 kV: gap >= 7.5 mm would be needed (worst of IEC F.2 case A 7.07 mm and M4 eta=0.3 7.46 mm)
NOT COVERED: flashover along the resistor body itself -> resistor pulse/ESD rating (datasheet), see calc_pulse_rated.py
RULE_4KV_MM=3.5
RULE_8KV_MM=7.5
